// @emit-error field access but no struct type declared
// A FLOOR PIN, and it was a CAST-FAILURE TRAP before the guard that produces this message.
//
// An arena type can carry more than ONE nominal name. `C = {kind: "circle", r: f64}` and
// `Ca = {kind: KC, r: f64}` are the SAME structure once the alias `KC = "circle"` folds, so
// with both unions in one module `nominalStructNameOfTy` answers whichever it finds first.
// The discriminant push narrowed `Ca | Ra` to the name `C`, and the emitter then cast the box
// to `C`'s variant heap type: `wasm trap: cast failure`.
//
// EACH UNION COMPILES AND RUNS CORRECTLY ON ITS OWN, which is exactly what kept this out of a
// per-program grid — the defect needs two structurally-alike unions in one module, and every
// cell of the single-union grid was green. It surfaced only when both were written into one
// fixture file.
//
// The bare `s is C` spelling never had the hole: it takes the SPELLING from the source. The
// discriminant has no spelling to take, so it checks the name it derived against the member
// set the receiver actually holds and declines when it is not there. Declining costs the
// narrowing and nothing else — the read falls to the shared-field plan, which refuses a field
// the other arms lack, and that refusal is the message pinned above.
//
// FLIPPING THIS is a real improvement and not a bug fix: resolve the surviving ARM rather than
// the surviving TYPE — walk the receiver's own member set and keep the atom whose arena type
// matches — so an ambiguous nominal name stops mattering. Pinned rather than guessed at,
// because nothing in the corpus exercised it.
type C = { kind: "circle", r: f64 }
type R = { kind: "rect", w: f64 }
type S = C | R
function area(s: S) {
  if s.kind == "circle" { return s.r }
  return 0.0
}

type KC = "circle"
type KR = "rect"
type Ca = { kind: KC, r: f64 }
type Ra = { kind: KR, w: f64 }
function areaA(s: Ca | Ra) {
  if s.kind == "circle" { return s.r }
  return 0.0
}

print(area({ kind: "circle", r: 3.0 }))
print(areaA({ kind: "circle", r: 9.0 }))
